"t":"ref","v":"Ps 83"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," This community lament asks God for rescue and victory. The terse poetry suggests difficult times. A powerful coalition desires to destroy Israel (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.83.1-4","r":"Ps.83.1-4","rawR":"Ps.83.1-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.83.1-4","value":"Ps.83.1-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"83:1-4"},") and allies itself against God (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.83.5-8","r":"Ps.83.5-8","rawR":"Ps.83.5-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.83.5-8","value":"Ps.83.5-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"83:5-8"},"). Recalling the fate of others who came against Israel (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.83.9-12","r":"Ps.83.9-12","rawR":"Ps.83.9-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.83.9-12","value":"Ps.83.9-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"83:9-12"},"), the psalmist prays that the same will happen to these enemies (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.83.13-16","r":"Ps.83.13-16","rawR":"Ps.83.13-16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.83.13-16","value":"Ps.83.13-16"}],"t":"ref","v":"83:13-16"},") so that God will receive honor among them (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.83.17-18","r":"Ps.83.17-18","rawR":"Ps.83.17-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.83.17-18","value":"Ps.83.17-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"83:17-18"},"). It is unclear whether this psalm arose out of a specific historical instance of opposition by these nations, or if it is a poetic collage of nations representing Israel’s enemies."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.83.1-18","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":83,"endVerse":18,"startChapter":83,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.83.1-18","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[83],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"b81f83d7c38e1fabe8feafb04bea46ad045ee022e176f0763fdc61973775a842","sourceItemName":"Ps.83.1-18","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6838,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.83.1-18","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.83.1-18","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.83.1-4","r":"Ps.83.1-4","rawR":"Ps.83.1-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.83.1-4","value":"Ps.83.1-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"83:1-4"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The enemy has successfully intimidated God’s people, so the poet prays that the Lord will hear and act."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.83.1-4","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":83,"endVerse":4,"startChapter":83,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.83.1-4","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[83],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"30f7c11bb1d8619cb93f5c556654ac0e083fed32c191930f2607ebb07d10e27f","sourceItemName":"Ps.83.1-4","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6839,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.83.1-4","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.83.1-4","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.83.5-8","r":"Ps.83.5-8","rawR":"Ps.83.5-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.83.5-8","value":"Ps.83.5-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"83:5-8"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["signed a treaty:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," The ",{"c":["allies"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," agreed to fight against God and his people. The nations that are named in the alliance were situated around Israel and Judah."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.83.5-8","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":83,"endVerse":8,"startChapter":83,"startVerse":5}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.83.5-8","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[83],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"3b98badf375eab97024321a00a853d1e0fb5e488e0d1260a942f3d36826eb0c7","sourceItemName":"Ps.83.5-8","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6840,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.83.5-8","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.83.5-8","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.83.6-7","r":"Ps.83.6-7","rawR":"Ps.83.6-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.83.6-7","value":"Ps.83.6-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"83:6-7"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The ",{"c":["Edomites"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},{"c":[","],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," descendants of Esau, were located to the southeast of Judah (see ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.25.30","r":"Gen.25.30","rawR":"Gen.25.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.25.30","value":"Gen.25.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gen 25:30"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.32.3","r":"Gen.32.3","rawR":"Gen.32.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.32.3","value":"Gen.32.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"32:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.36.1-8","r":"Gen.36.1-8","rawR":"Gen.36.1-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.36.1-8","value":"Gen.36.1-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"36:1-8"},"). • ",{"c":["Ishmaelites"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," were desert-dwelling descendants of Hagar. • ",{"c":["Moabites"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," and ",{"c":["Ammonites"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," descended from Lot; both were located to the east of Israel and Judah. • The ",{"c":["Hagrites"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," were possibly located north of the Ammonites (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.5.10","r":"1Chr.5.10","rawR":"1Chr.5.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.5.10","value":"1Chr.5.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 5:10"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.83.6-7","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":83,"endVerse":7,"startChapter":83,"startVerse":6}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.83.6-7","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[83],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"3f41084cbba9b254310050497041c8c06936b377cdda6d72810546ab6d73cbc8","sourceItemName":"Ps.83.6-7","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6841,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.83.6-7","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.83.6-7","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.83.7","r":"Ps.83.7","rawR":"Ps.83.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.83.7","value":"Ps.83.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"83:7"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The ",{"c":["Gebalites"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," probably came from Gebal/Byblos on the coast of Lebanon. • The ",{"c":["Amalekites"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," were located south of Israel in the Negev. • ",{"c":["Philistia"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," was southwest of Judah, by the Mediterranean Sea. • ",{"c":["Tyre"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," was a port city on the Mediterranean, northwest of Israel."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.83.7","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":83,"endVerse":7,"startChapter":83,"startVerse":7}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.83.7","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[83],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"a4f3452bc95c0719132e81b9e01d6a3607c543c57a81c09e50360416d5b8cd6b","sourceItemName":"Ps.83.7","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6842,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.83.7","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.83.7","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.83.8","r":"Ps.83.8","rawR":"Ps.83.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.83.8","value":"Ps.83.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"83:8"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["Assyria"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," was northeast of Israel and north of the Persian Gulf. • The ",{"c":["descendants of Lot"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," were the Moabites and the Ammonites (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.83.6-7","r":"Ps.83.6-7","rawR":"Ps.83.6-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.83.6-7","value":"Ps.83.6-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"83:6-7"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.83.8","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":83,"endVerse":8,"startChapter":83,"startVerse":8}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.83.8","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[83],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"8396035b9f0591e96b6d049bc1fea0a3347b23c0319dc1ab32be795c0d681d16","sourceItemName":"Ps.83.8","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":6843,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.83.8","sourceRelease":"1.25",